":"2026-02-16T16:24:54Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115877","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115877","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115877.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115877.patch","merged_at":"2026-02-16T16:24:54Z"},"body":"This bumps Jolt Physics from jrouwe/JoltPhysics@036ea7b1d717b3e713ac9d8cbd47118fb9cd5d60 (version 5.4.0) to jrouwe/JoltPhysics@23dadd0e603f1b321142d4c74df07fce85064989 (version 5.5.0).\r\n\r\nThis is mostly in the interest of not drifting too far away from the latest point release, since we're backporting stuff from the unreleased version already, but looking at the changes and the [release notes](https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/releases/tag/v5.5.0) I get the sense that there might be one or two bug fixes in here that might still be relevant to Godot in rare edge-cases.\r\n\r\nNote that this should (unless I messed something up) still include the changes we've already backported from the unreleased version of Jolt, which consists of:\r\n\r\n1. [jrouwe/JoltPhysics#1879](https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/pull/1879), which was backported in #115089.\r\n2. [jrouwe/JoltPhysics#1890](https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/pull/1890), which was backported in #115305.\r\n3. [jrouwe/JoltPhysics@365a153](https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/commit/365a15367e334300c4e87e6dfc8bfe08f163ebae), which was backported in #115305.\r\n4. [jrouwe/JoltPhysics#1893](https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/pull/1893), which was backported in #115327.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"h